# JOURNEY · fish with an Angler Rig: a rail casts once, the player's one Bait goes down, something comes up.
# Rod's coil makes it a rail on go, which is also its rig's cast: it rises once, from the cold first stage.
# The line waits for a bite as a human's does (2 s, then about 5 s more), so the play slows the world to
# one second a tick first. caught is high for one stage only, so Bell, a bare botfish that hears caught and
# its own output, latches it: Bell's dot lights in /circuit once the catch is in.
# Spent: Computer $8000 + Inverter Coil $496 + Angler Rig $7700 + two botfish $15400 = $31596 of the
# 40,000 stake (scenes/start-with-a-stake.play), and the one Bait is bought at the counter.
# Rod's panel walks by count: listens, drives, threshold, cast, caught.

clear
include scenes/start-with-a-stake.play
include scenes/grow-a-matrixtank.play
include scenes/buy-at-the-bench.play "Inverter Coil" Fabric
include scenes/buy-at-the-bench.play "Angler Rig" Hands
include scenes/buy-a-fish.play Botfish rod
include scenes/buy-a-fish.play Botfish bell

run /shop
key enter
select Bait
key enter
expect < 1 >
snap one bait on the counter
key enter
key esc
key esc
absent Price/unit

run /consume inverter coil
key enter
run /consume angler rig
expect Angler Rig to the botfishes
snap the install picker offers the Angler Rig to Rod
key enter
absent to the botfishes

run /program "Bell"
type caught, held
key down
type held
snap Bell hears caught and holds itself up
key enter
absent listens

run /fps 1
run /program "Rod"
expect threshold
key down
type go
key down 2
type go
key down
type caught
snap Rod is a rail on go, which casts its rig once
key enter
absent listens

tick 100
run /circuit
expect ●  Bell
snap Bell caught the pulse the rig raised when something came up
key esc
absent Circuit#
